        {
            "id": "37243569-3c45-464a-80e4-94994b51d9c3",
            "type": "sourceText",
            "position": {
                "x": 1280,
                "y": -360
            },
            "size": {
                "width": 320,
                "height": 260
            },
            "config": {
                "text": "Mobile game UI/UX design, level failed screen, pop-up modal window for a premium casual word puzzle game. Juicy 3D, warm and rich art style.\n\nBackground: A blurred, slightly dimmed magical library with dark wooden bookshelves to create a dramatic mood.\n\nThe Main Pop-up Window: A large, thick panel with a light-wooden frame and a rich purple/blue gradient interior (matching the reference).\nTop: Bold 3D text \"CONTINUE?\" centered. A glossy red circular \"X\" close button in the top right corner.\n\nCenter Panel: Below the title, an inset beige parchment panel with metallic studs in the corners. Inside this panel is a glossy blue ribbon banner featuring a large golden text \"+5\". Below the banner, the text \"Add 5 moves and continue!\".\n\nAction Buttons: Exactly TWO large horizontal glossy buttons side-by-side at the bottom of the pop-up.\n\nLeft button: Bright green, with a gold coin icon and the text \"900\".\n\nRight button: Amber-orange, with a blue video play icon and the text \"PLAY FOR AD\".\n\nBottom Banner: At the very bottom of the screen, a horizontal promo banner for the \"Season Pass\" featuring a golden ticket, small 3D chests, and a green \"Activate\" button.\n\nHigh contrast, vibrant colors, light wood, purple and blue accents, rich background, clean layout, 8k --ar 9:16 --no three stacked buttons, washed out colors, overexposed background, dark ornate wood, realistic animals",
                "sourceName": ""
            },
            "inputs": [],
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "id": "291dcca3-255f-480f-a65c-7f636e43a18f",
                    "name": "out",
                    "type": "text"
                }
            ]
        },
